<title>USA: St Joseph hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs up $1.00 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Tuesday, barrows and gilts were $1.00 higher. Top $51.50 per cwt.</p>
<p>Two days of sharply lower price trends curtailed marketings. Relatively liberal slaughter for a Holiday Monday, big kill Tuesday and packers beginning to need hogs again.</p>
<p>With current kill capacity it did not take long to clean up adverse weather backlog of marketings.</p>
<p>    US 1-3    230-270 lbs    51.00-51.50</p>
<p>    US 2-3    270-290 lbs    49.50-50.50</p>
<p>    US 2-4    290-310 lbs    47.50-48.50</p>
<p>Sows - steady. Top $49.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2    300-500 lbs    42.50</p>
<p>    US 1-3    500-550 lbs    46.00</p>
<p>		  550-700 lbs    48.00-49.00</p>
<p>    Boars -   300-700 lbs    39.50</p>
<p>		  200-300 lbs    40.50</p>
</text>
